  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNPBF - MOUFHED</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project capacitates and strengthens&#xa0;at-risk rural women&apos;s leadership in two conflict affected departments of Haiti, North-East and South,&#xa0;tackling the systemic exclusion of women from Natural Resources Management (NRM) processes&#xa0;on land and land rights. Compounding vulnerabilities have resulted in direct and structural violence&#xa0;against women and young women (18-34), deeply impacted by the insecurity, gender, climate nexus.
Adopting a human-centered, feminist peacebuilding approach, the project strengthens women,&#xa0;women&#x2019;s organizations, networks and informal structures, ensures access to justice, safe structures&#xa0;to engage constructively in policy processes, provides opportunities for green social and economic&#xa0;leadership, and builds rural women&#x2019;s agency as catalysts for sustainable peace, within a highly&#xa0;patriarchal Haitian society. This amplifies the voice and influence of at-risk rural women, bolstering&#xa0;civil society &#x2013; state relations, as guarantors of women&apos;s land rights and bolsters accountability to&#xa0;ensure non-repetition, with tangible dividends for sustainable peace.
MOUFHED will be responsible for all the gender and social justice aspects for women and young people in the project.</narrative>
  </description>
